      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the OAuth Callback**\n\nOkay, I'm setting up a `oauth_callback.py` Python file to manage the OAuth/OIDC callback process, crucial for exchanging the authorization code for tokens. I've decided to move forward with Google as the external provider, making the code more concrete and manageable. I'm focusing on incorporating this into the structure.\n\n\n**Implementing the Callback Handler**\n\nI'm now fully immersed in the `oauth_callback.py` file, focusing on the callback handler implementation. My priority is getting the authorization code exchange process right with Google's API. I'm actively integrating Google's token exchange endpoint and parameters like the client ID, secret, redirect URI, and grant type into the code. The objective is to make all API calls with Google.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860394110,
          "start": 1789860391717
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bbfe2b25001BYtNRYOhh3EmNa",
      "message_id": "msg_0bbfe2650001dTY6s6aKFGJAbs",
      "session_id": "ses_f4401d9daffeU5vx0FjQ1R0U4O",
      "time_created": 1789860391717,
      "time_updated": 1789860394110
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "9I4yiNbX7zQOdIjO",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "\nimport os\nimport requests\n\n# Google OAuth 2.0 Token Endpoint\nGOOGLE_TOKEN_ENDPOINT = \"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token\"\n\ndef handle_oauth_callback(authorization_code: str, redirect_uri: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles the OAuth/OIDC callback and exchanges an authorization code for tokens.\n\n    Args:\n        authorization_code: The authorization code received from the identity provider.\n        redirect_uri: The redirect URI used in the initial authorization request.\n\n    Returns:\n        A dictionary containing the tokens (access_token, id_token, etc.) or an error.\n    \"\"\"\n    client_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\")\n    client_secret = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET\")\n\n    if not client_id or not client_secret:\n        raise ValueError(\"GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET must be set as environment variables.\")\n\n    payload = {\n        \"code\": authorization_code,\n        \"client_id\": client_id,\n        \"client_secret\": client_secret,\n        \"redirect_uri\": redirect_uri,\n        \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\",\n    }\n\n    try:\n        response = requests.post(GOOGLE_TOKEN_ENDPOINT, data=payload)\n        response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an HTTPError for bad responses (4xx or 5xx)\n        return response.json()\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n        return {\"error\": str(e)}\n\n",
            "filePath": "oauth_callback.py"
          },
